a  put up on from the report of the number  of women who said they were assaulted  it's just staggering  well i can't say enough about uh nora's  reporting and the investigative team and  the producers who worked with her  they've been working on it for over a  year and a half and kudos to uh  secretary mccarthy because he knew  he was walking into a bus saw i'm not  calling nora bus saw what i'm saying  there is that  she and her team have felt very  passionate about it he knew the  questions were not going to be easy he  knew he had some  very difficult questions to answer and  he still sat down and he seemed  to me personally agreed by it he talked  about having a daughter himself  but i still go back to vanessa guillen  and her family if the family hadn't  spoken up the way that they did they  refused to just let this he was a leader  here he didn't run and hide  when the reporting came out he sat in  the chair and he said we're going to  make changes and the fact that he wants  to do it before january so it can be him  and not the next person  is big and they are sweeping changes
 

